{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774749,"nonce":"WhRjo7wPA5LCa0N2WbeIQfzaTu0=","title":"Master-key rotation: fingerprinted KEKs, one-arm stamped reads, converging rewrap (f37463a)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #104 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/f37463a-master-key-rotation` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-08-26T11:57:19Z · Merged: 2026-08-26T13:10:49Z\n\nMaster-key rotation for the secrets store (git-bug `f37463a`) — the last item in the security cluster. **912/912 green.** Full chain: design → skeptical audit → independent judge → build → crypto-lens review (all clean, three LOW polish notes).\n\n**Before:** `SCARAB_MASTER_KEY` could never change — no row recorded which key wrapped it, so a new key made every secret undecryptable with nothing better than a GCM tag failure.\n\n**Now:**\n- `SCARAB_MASTER_KEYS=\"\u003cnew-b64\u003e,\u003cold-b64\u003e\"` — first key writes, the rest decrypt. Key identity is a self-verifying fingerprint (8-byte truncated SHA-256 of the key bytes): operators can't mislabel keys, and errors name provable identities — \"row sealed under `a1b2…`, configured: [`c3d4…`]\".\n- Rows are stamped with their wrapping key's fingerprint; **stamped rows decrypt in exactly one arm** (AAD-bound, exact key) so a tag failure there *means* corruption. Legacy NULL rows keep the trial ladder with an honest error (\"pre-rotation key absent, **or** the row is corrupt — GCM cannot distinguish\").\n- Rotation converges two ways: rewrap-on-read, and a boot sweep on every replica (batched, one row in memory at a time, CAS-guarded so a concurrent write always wins — the race is constructed in a test, not scheduled). The sweep also drains the PR #96 legacy-AAD debt: an empty-AAD row is upgraded whole in ONE UPDATE, preserving \"stamped ⇒ AAD-bound\" through every crash.\n- **Upgrades cannot brick** (the audit's one BLOCKS, judge-ruled): the legacy `SCARAB_MASTER_KEY` may coexist with the list iff its bytes are a member — the list is authoritative, a non-active member warns \"drop SCARAB_MASTER_KEY\", a non-member refuses loudly naming both fingerprints. The chart `fail`s at template time only when both chart *values* are set.\n- Confirmation surface: the startup report's KEK line (fingerprints only — `MasterKeySet`'s Debug is fingerprint-only by construction), the sweep's summary log, and the `scarab_secrets_rows_under_nonactive_key` gauge. Zero = safe to drop the old key.\n\nRotate: add new key at the head, keep old in the list → deploy (sweep rewraps, reads catch stragglers) → gauge reads 0 → drop the old key.\n\nReview polish notes (LOW, non-blocking): value-ciphertext corruption on a stamped row reports the generic message (only wrap corruption gets the specific one); `rewrap_row`'s doc could state its snapshot must come from the DB; dev-insecure boots sweep-log expected debris at debug.\n\nCloses `f37463a` on merge. Future hooks noted in the crate doc: `key_id` is exactly where a KMS ARN would go.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n\n\n**@thulasi-ram** — 2026-08-26T12:54:54Z\n\nRebased onto main (now containing #102/#103/#105-base). The conflict was purely additive — #102's expiry metrics and this branch's rotation gauge landed at the same spots in metrics.rs; both kept. Full suite on the rebased branch: **942/942** (the count grew because main brought the retention + Cache + warm-bound tests along).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}